WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.620
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.330
the Kingdom of Chin launched
an invasion of the land of Gi.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.330
Their opponent: the legendary general Ren Pa.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.160
The young commanders stepped
onto a relentless battlefield,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.790
their sights set on a major victory.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:02.750
And now I'll take <i>your</i> life...
Mr. Thousand-Man-Commander-For-A-Day.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.410
Defend Ou Hon!

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.700
I wonder if you can!

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.080
Move.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.250
S-Sir?

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.160
I've got this.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.040
"Gen Pou's Cunning Scheme"

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.370
The first unit is struggling!

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.500
En Bi's and Tai Un's squads
have been destroyed!

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.500
General Do Mon has taken up arms himself,

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.410
and is now standing on the front lines!

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:52.410
T-Two thousand-men squads down--
just like that?!

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.120
Wait...

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.500
Weren't En Bi and Tai Un
both last-minute commanders?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.370
So the ad-hoc thousand-man
commanders aren't fit for real battle?

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.910
What's going on with the Gyoku Hou Force?

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.370
Huh, messenger guy?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.120
Like I know!

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.160
Who the hell are you, anyway?!

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.250
Ou Hon...

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.250
Single combat, hmm?

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.790
No, thanks.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.410
All right, men--

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.160
Make quick work of them.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.830
Wh-What?!

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:46.830
Here they come!

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.160
Wh-What might...

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.580
This has nothing to do with
coordination within the squad.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:06.040
This enemy is frighteningly strong!

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.370
This squad isn't like the rest.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.870
There must be two, three hundred
elites among them.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:18.620
Though surely even they have
far less experience than my men.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.830
In any case, our squad

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.750
is under Rin Ko, one of the Big Four

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.790
directly attached to General Ren Pa,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.500
who fought through and survived

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.450
the era of Sho's first Three Greats

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.830
and Chin's six great generals.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.750
One of Ren Pa's... Big Four?

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.870
It makes no difference.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.410
No matter how strong your troops,
take out their commander

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.120
and the squad will be destroyed.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.540
Then it's all over.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.750
That's true, yes.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.250
You've got a point there.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:10.330
And if you want it that badly...
well, no hard feelings.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.290
General Do Mon, don't push yourself too hard!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.620
I know!

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:23.790
My standing at the fore has
revitalized the troops a little...

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:30.620
But losing two of eight thousand troops
so quickly is too big a blow.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.950
Sir! May I suggest falling back
for now and regrouping?

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.120
No!

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.080
Victory for these once
identically-sized vanguards

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.290
depends greatly on the morale
of all troops on both sides!

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.120
We <i>will</i> turn the tide of this battle,
no matter what!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.870
I'll visit the squads that are hurting
to give them inspiration!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.370
Come with me!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.370
Yes, sir!

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.500
Second unit, prepare to sally forth!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.080
Take your positions!

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.130
"Ei Bi, General of Chin"

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.540
What can I say?

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.870
Time to clean up the first unit's mess!

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.910
Hi Shin Unit!

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.200
Is Shin here?

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.870
Huh? Y-Yeah!

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.290
The first unit's status is as reported.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:24.450
The enemy's probably going after the
ad-hoc thousand-man commanders.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:26.580
Which means...

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.700
you better damn well understand
that your Hi Shin Unit

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.450
is next in line!

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:35.660
Don't go down too fast, now.
It'd inconvenience the rest of us!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.660
Same goes for you, Jou Han!

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.870
Y-Yessir!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.200
Just what I wanted!

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.200
You good over there? Let's get a move on!

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.750
Sir!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.120
So Sui, is the cavalry ready?

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.200
Okay!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.200
En?

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:02.870
Always!

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.700
Good!

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:05.700
Kyou Kai?

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.040
Check!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.620
Let's do this!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.500
Second unit! Go!

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.870
The second unit is on the move!
Commanding general, Ei Bi!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.290
Eight thousand troops--two thousand of which

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:42.540
are the ad-hoc thousand-man
Fei Shin and Jou Han Forces!

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:47.660
Oop!

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.410
Rin Ko can't get near him!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.330
That's Ou Hon for you!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.910
Yes--it's totally one-sided!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.160
N-No, that's not it...

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.540
Ou Hon's been dealing
some full-powered thrusts

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.700
the likes of which we rarely see in battle.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.870
And yet...

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:14.750
that man's body hasn't a single scratch.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.500
What a surprise!

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:22.500
I've fought with countless spearmen in my day,

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.080
but you--you stand above the rest.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.620
Those spear skills!

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.200
You're young, but your
proficiency comes through.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.870
It's only natural.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.120
That unflagging energy...

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:39.000
He may have been born with
an innate talent for the spear,

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.540
but he was never arrogant about it.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:49.120
His hands split, their blood spurted,
and snow was made vapor in its heat.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.950
Ou Hon, given a daredevil
warrior's incessant training

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:55.040
from an early age,

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.790
wields the spear as though already an expert!

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.700
He's getting even faster.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:05.700
There it is!

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:06.700
It's...

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.290
...the Dragon Finger!

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.500
He...

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.370
...He did it!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.200
No...

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.700
He missed!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.040
At first I wasn't entirely sure
that I'd dodged it...

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.660
but as I said, when you've
fought with enough spearmen,

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:37.750
you tend to see these kinds
of tricks a time or two.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:39.450
And, well...

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.580
Did you know?

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.660
Right after a major move like that,

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.160
there's <i>always</i> an opening.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:52.830
H-His sword!

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.450
When did he throw that?!

00:09:56.410 --> 00:10:00.700
Seems the Chin army has <i>lots</i>
of ambitious young fellows these days.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.040
But see...

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.120
<i>You</i> were unlucky.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.620
My spear--it's bent in two!

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.540
How strong <i>is</i> this scoundrel?!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:32.580
Fall back for now, Gyoku Hou Force!
Get in front of Ou Hon!

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:35.370
Now, <i>that</i> won't work!
I won't let you get away.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.870
Don't pull out blindly!
You'll just be hit from behind.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.330
Sir!

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.000
We stay here and we fight!

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.580
Next time, I won't miss.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.950
My, my!

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.120
What's that rumbling?

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.500
The Chin army's second unit!

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.080
We're comin', vanguard!

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.790
Rin Ko, sir!
The enemy's second unit is approaching

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:15.450
with about eight thousand!

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.830
We're making contact!

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:24.830
General Ren Pa, we should send out
our own reinforcements soon.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.250
No need.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.950
Keep sending out these defective armies

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:33.580
and we'll just keep getting the same result.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:39.000
"Rin Ko"

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:50.120
Commander Jou Han!
The first unit has been split up!

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:51.870
The seventh unit is destroyed!

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.200
The eighth unit, too!

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.370
Send the fourth unit out in front!

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.160
The fourth unit?

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.080
There <i>is</i> no fourth unit!

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.200
What?!

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.290
A squad's strength on the battlefield depends on

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:09.160
a unified consciousness
and precise coordination.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.410
Without these, a squad
cannot demonstrate its power,

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.080
whether offensive or defensive.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.250
The enemy cavalry is approaching!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.580
If even the Gyoku Hou Force was struggling,

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.950
the rest of the ad-hoc squads
were finding it impossible

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.950
to fight well in a real battle.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.910
Ei Bi, sir! Jou Han's
squad is in a tight spot!

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:31.120
Send help! Mmm... so they're no good...

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.000
What about the Hi Shin Unit?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.950
They've also been split--

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:42.120
But one strange thing: alone among them all,

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.250
the Hi Shin Unit gave off an intense light!

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.040
Go!

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.160
What's that?

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:10.500
Rin Ko, sir--there's shouting off to the left.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:11.580
I hear it.

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.870
What an odd upsurge...

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.370
The shouts came from this side!

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.500
Which squad?

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:23.160
The Hi Shin Unit.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.660
Wh-What the hell is with these guys?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.620
That's one mixed-up squad--
and with not a speck of coordination

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.910
between infantry and cavalry.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.750
So why haven't they been destroyed?

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.620
How can they be this strong?!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:44.500
No, they're not just mixed up... they're--

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.540
There was a trick to the
Hi Shin Unit's actions that day.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:58.200
And next, if we in the cavalry are here...

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.580
the infantry moves down along
here and circles around to here.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:06.500
At the same time, split into two,
with one half following the cavalry.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:11.910
But watch here and here.
If the enemy shows up here, we have to--

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.750
Let's just forget about it, So Sui.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:20.330
We got plenty of faith in our brawn,
but we're not so great at brains.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:26.870
There's no use springin' a joint
attack plan on us. It's bound to fail.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:32.950
It'd be even better if we fought separately.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.580
We can handle bein' on our own,

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.620
and I'm sure you Kaku Bi folks
won't have any problems.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.540
B-But then what's the point
of our being a thousand-man--

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:44.450
No... I think Shin's right about this.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.700
Even I had the feeling as I was explaining it

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.160
that we couldn't fight that way.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.160
All right. Let's forget about all that for now.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.540
Just one thing...

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:01.000
Let's go out there as a thousand-man unit

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.660
with one very simple,
very easy arrangement in mind.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:05.660
An arrangement?

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.660
That is...

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:12.410
The flag!

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.080
The arrangement held that

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.580
given the signal,

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:21.290
at any time, fighting any foe,

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:25.830
Commander Shin would set
his sights on the agreed-upon enemy

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:28.290
and all one thousand troops

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.910
would attack as one!

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.290
Wow! What raw destructive power!
Their main force went flying!

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:37.870
I've never seen anything like it!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.290
Shin!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:40.290
Yep!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.330
You bet we've never had
that kind of power before!

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:47.950
If we can fight like that
with one simple tactic...

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:52.120
imagine what this unit'd be
if we really came together as one!

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:54.620
That's not all a thousand-man unit can do!

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:57.700
So Sui!

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.160
Look around you.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:06.120
The offensive power of the Hi Shin Unit
is spreading to the others,

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:09.500
and the whole Chin army is starting to rally!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:13.500
G-General Ren Pa, sir... what is all this?!

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.330
All right! Time to go all out!

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.080
Rin Ko, sir, the action's over there.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.410
That's odd...

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:29.660
To think the Gi army could
lose the upper hand so easily...

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:33.750
There must be a real live wire
in Chin's second unit.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.790
All right, let's cut him down!

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:36.790
Yes, sir!

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:45.200
Wh-What the hell is that deafening sound?

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.700
What's goin' on?!

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.580
A gong?

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:55.910
It's a signal.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:56.910
A signal?!

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.200
What, already?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.700
Here they come:

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.580
The enemy's second unit...

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.120
General Ren Pa, what's that sound?

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.500
If you think Ren Pa would send
a second unit of mere reinforcements,

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.580
you're greatly mistaken!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.450
Look at that, Haku Ki Sai!

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.330
He's got this early battle in the bag.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:29.290
What's keepin' 'em?
If you're gonna come, come already!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.830
It--It stopped!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.580
Smoke?!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.750
The battlefield is enveloped in smoke!

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.040
Are they setting fires?

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:05.750
No--there's no fire,
just smoke covering the field!

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:09.250
A smokescreen? And on such a huge scale?

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.620
Shin! Are you all right?

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:15.870
So Sui!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:21.580
We're through. With no visibility,
everyone's stopped dead.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.580
Dammit! Just when we were on a roll!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.000
It must be an enemy strategy.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:32.870
You think this'll stop us? Don't kid yourselves!

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:36.370
As if a little break in fighting
will change the tide of battle!

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:38.080
As soon as it clears up, we'll--

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:40.830
Wow, they're furious!

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:44.410
But here's where it starts getting <i>really</i> scary.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.330
Fire!

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:56.120
Get down!

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:03.830
This is absurd! Are they insane,
taking out their allies like that?!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.790
The Gi soldiers--they've disappeared!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.500
Dammit! We have to back down!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.200
No, they're behind us, too!

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.830
What?!

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:16.500
The smoke is moving with the soldiers.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:18.870
Does the Gi army plan on fighting in this?!

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.160
Let's change our location!

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:26.200
The enemy is memorizing where
we've been and attacking those spots!

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:30.950
So if we take a new position
in all this smoke, they'll lose us?

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:33.450
All right, Hi Shin Unit--let's move!

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:37.830
We might encounter the enemy
on the way! Be careful!

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.910
Go!

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:46.200
The Gyoku Hou and other squads
were also on the move.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.660
The Gi archers couldn't see the Chin squads,

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.000
and it was impossible to tell
where they were headed

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.950
from their footsteps alone.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:54.950
However...

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:00.040
Wh-What?!

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:03.910
The Gi archers had
accurately tracked the Chin army

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:07.450
through the zero-visibility smoke.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:11.700
Kyo Gai! Dammit!

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.370
What the hell is going on?!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:14.790
How can this be?

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.950
Yep--one big ol' ball of confusion!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.370
So, nothing left for me to do
in this early stage?

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.700
After all...

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.660
once they get caught up in <i>his</i> techniques,

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.410
there's no escaping them.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:34.950
Gen Pou, sir! Nothing unusual to report!

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:37.160
I know that! Save your breath!

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.200
This is too easy.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:46.200
Just bring it out, would you?

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.250
Already, sir?!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:50.370
Stop asking questions and bring it out!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:56.370
Honestly! Every country's the same:
nothing but idiots!

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:58.830
Especially those Chin soldiers...

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:02.870
getting all flustered over such a simple tactic.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:08.250
What a bore. Is there no one
out there with half a brain?

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.160
I get it...

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:25.700
So that's how it is.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:34.290
Where do we go?

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:35.870
It's the same everywhere.

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:38.290
Kyou Kai!

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:41.910
They're using sound to figure out our position.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.120
Sound?!

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:47.660
There are troops hidden all around us,
sending out signals with sound.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:52.910
They move when we move,
telling the archers our location.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:53.870
What?!

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:57.700
Y-You know, I <i>have</i> heard
a bell mixed in with all the noise...

00:21:57.700 --> 00:22:00.660
So if we get rid of those troops,
we get rid of the arrows!

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:04.000
But they'll be expecting us to do just that.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:08.700
We could cut them down and they'd
just be replaced. It'd never end.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:17.330
Worse, we've already lost track
of most of our allies in this smoke,

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:21.120
but the Gi troops know exactly
where everyone is--friend <i>and</i> foe.

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:25.120
They'll be stamping out the
small scattered units one by one.

00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:27.290
We've got to get out of this smoke and--

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:31.950
What can <i>that</i> be signaling?

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.080
No--wait!

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:36.450
That's no signal!

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:40.450
D-Do you mean... no! Can it be?

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:41.660
I-I'm afraid so...

00:22:42.910 --> 00:22:44.450
Uh-oh...

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:48.200
Armored Gi chariots!

00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:54.330
Shit! Hey, you! Get outta there!

00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:00.910
War chariots, of all things!

00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:02.290
Protect our commander!

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:05.330
Nevermind me--protect the infantry!

00:23:06.660 --> 00:23:09.950
War chariots, in this smoke? Now what?

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:11.540
How can we...

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:12.540
Shin.

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:15.370
There's only one--

00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:18.580
Only one way through this.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"The Hi Shin Unit Retaliates"
